\label{sec:ratio}

It is tempting to report that content closure removes most of the
capacity. That figure is not stable, and this project has watched it
move. Raising the per-attribute search ceilings from hand-chosen values
to ones derived from the substrate's own constants changed the
open-rung total from $\geq$4297 bits to {{OPEN_BITS}} and the
content-rung sum from $\geq$201 to {{CONTENT_BITS}} --- while the
substrate itself was not touched. A percentage built on either pair
would have moved with it, and a reader could not tell the movement of
