fraction content closure appears to remove slides from
{{CEIL_FRAC_MIN}} to {{CEIL_FRAC_MAX}} --- a factor of three --- as the
ceiling rises, and plateaus only once it passes the substrate's own
limit. The joint residual, measured by the same encoder and never
touching the content cell, holds at {{CEIL_RESIDUAL}} bits throughout. A
percentage reported from any single ceiling is a reading of the
